[all_together_subsections] parent=Experiments sample=2 attempt=1/7
Here is the list of results:

1. Fairness on dataset summarization task: FMC achieves zero unfairness, standard sampling method exhibits significantly higher unfairness
2. Average size of -nets: FMC introduces a minimal increase in sample size compared to standard approach (logarithmic to 2)
3. Runtime comparison: FMC runs in only 0.3 seconds for k=1M, confirming its scalability
4. GLP v.s. FGLP on PopSim dataset: FGLP reduces unfairness 45 times while maintaining a comparable sample size
5. Hitting set algorithms: FGLP achieves zero unfairness with minimal increase in runtime
6. Geometric Set Cover: FGLP achieves zero unfairness with only a minimal increase in runtime
7. Rank Regret Representatives: Consistent results across different values of = 
8. Unfairness on larger dataset size: FMC maintains its fairness advantage even at larger dataset sizes
